Dependency disclosure
=======================================================================

Aevom installs further third-party packages rather than copying their source.
Each remains under its own license, which is not reproduced here.

The tables below list the packages Aevom names directly in its requirements
files, package.json dependencies and Dockerfiles, with the version installed
in Aevom's images. Packages that these depend on are not listed, nor are
build-only and test-only tools. Image names are abbreviated:

  api        backend/Dockerfile, which also bundles the frontend
  rdkit, pyexec, vina, vina-gpu, admet, plip, molstar
             the services/ image of the same name (molstar is
             services/molstar-headless)
  training   the training images built from training/slurm/container/
  worker     the GPU conformer worker at /opt/aevom-conformer-worker in the
             vina-gpu and training images

The training images are built on NeMo-RL, whose own components are not
listed here. They also install backend/requirements.txt, so they contain the
api packages, resolved against NeMo-RL's environment.

