Packages with terms beyond attribution
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Arize Phoenix (arize-phoenix, arize-phoenix-evals): Elastic License 2.0.
  The api image includes them as Python libraries, and the Helm chart and
  Compose files run the upstream arizephoenix/phoenix:version-13.0.3 image.
  Elastic License 2.0 is not an open-source license. It does not permit
  providing the software to third parties as a hosted or managed service
  that gives them access to a substantial set of its features, circumventing
  its license-key functionality, or removing its licensing notices.

Open Babel (openbabel-wheel) and PLIP: GPL-2.0.
  Both are installed unmodified from PyPI, Open Babel in the pyexec, vina,
  vina-gpu and training images and PLIP in the plip image. GPL-2.0 requires
  copies of them to be accompanied by the license text and by the
  corresponding source code or a written offer for it. Source:
  https://github.com/openbabel/openbabel and https://github.com/pharmai/plip

Meeko: LGPL-2.1.
  Installed unmodified from PyPI in the vina, vina-gpu and training images,
  where it remains a separate, replaceable Python package. Source:
  https://github.com/forlilab/Meeko

gemmi and Eigen: MPL-2.0.
  gemmi is installed unmodified from PyPI in the vina, vina-gpu, plip and
  training images. Eigen is a header-only library compiled, unmodified, into
  nvMolKit in the conformer worker. MPL-2.0 applies file by file, and
  distributing either in executable form requires telling recipients where
  to obtain the source: https://github.com/project-gemmi/gemmi and
  https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen

